{
  "_comment": [
    "Content-addressed identity vectors, shared by two implementations:",
    "  packages/core/src/attestation/{pae,id}.rs   (Rust, canonical)",
    "  packages/hub/internal/contentaddress        (Go, ingestion gate)",
    "",
    "Generated by running the Rust implementation. Not hand-computed -- a",
    "hand-computed vector tests whether two people made the same mistake.",
    "",
    "  PAE    = 'DSSEv1 ' + len(type) + ' ' + type + ' ' + len(payload)",
    "           + ' ' + payload      (payload = RAW decoded bytes)",
    "  art_id = 'art_' + hex(sha256(PAE)[:16])",
    "  digest = 'sha256:' + hex(sha256(PAE))",
    "",
    "payload_b64 is base64url WITHOUT padding, as it appears in a DSSE",
    "envelope. PAE covers the decoded bytes; hashing the base64 string",
    "instead yields a plausible ID that never matches a real one.",
    "",
    "The multibyte case is load-bearing: PAE lengths are BYTE counts, so an",
    "implementation using character counts passes every ASCII vector and",
    "fails only on real payloads."
  ],
